<h3>About Tesla Fleet API Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the register button, you will be redirected to <b>accounts.tesla.com</b> (Tesla's official identity portal):</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your Tesla Fleet account</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, offline_access, vehicle_data)</li>
<li>Complete the fleet telematics registration</li>
<li>Upload vehicle GPS and route data</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FBE9E7;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we need GPS and route patterns:</b> Tesla's fleet charging AI optimizes when and where your vehicles charge based on their driving patterns and nearby Supercharger availability. This reduces fleet charging costs by an average of 23%. The vehicle_data scope includes location, battery state, and charging history — all necessary for the optimization engine. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-vehicle registration (28 vehicles × VIN + telematics data = typically 30-40 minutes). This is standard for all Tesla Fleet API integrations.
</p>

<h3>五、What Happens If You Miss Friday</h3>
<ul>
<li>Fleet Supercharger rate reverts to <b>retail pricing</b> ($0.40/kWh, 67% higher)</li>
<li>Additional $336/month per vehicle ($9,408/month total increase)</li>
<li>Existing charge history retained (no data loss)</li>
<li>Re-enrollment available next billing cycle (December 7)</li>
</ul>

